---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const title = 'About Room Planner';
const description =
  'Room Planner is a free, browser-based 2D room and furniture layout tool. No account, no download, and your layouts stay on your own device.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/about">
  <section class="rp-container py-12">
    <div class="rp-prose">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">About Room Planner</h1>

      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Room Planner exists to answer one question quickly: where should the furniture go?
      </p>

      <h2>Why it is deliberately simple</h2>
      <p>
        Most room-planning tools are either too basic to be useful or so complete that you have to learn
        them first. Room Planner aims at the middle: draw a rectangular room, drop in furniture at real
        sizes, and drag it around until the layout works. Most people get to a usable bedroom plan in under
        a minute.
      </p>
      <p>
        That means some things are intentionally left out. There are no 3D walkthroughs, no material
        libraries, no lighting simulation, and no polygon wall editing. Those belong in a CAD package, and
        if you need one, you should use one.
      </p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Everything runs in your browser. There is no server doing the drawing, no account to create, and
        nothing to install. Your work is saved in your browser's own storage, which is why layouts stay on
        the device you made them on — and why exporting a layout file is the way to move one elsewhere.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Room Planner is exactly as accurate as the numbers you give it. Internally everything is stored in
        a single unit and converted only for display, so switching between feet and metres never drifts.
        What it cannot do is check your tape measure — so measure twice, and verify anything critical
        before you buy.
      </p>

      <h2>How it is funded</h2>
      <p>
        The planner is free. It is intended to be supported by advertising on the surrounding pages. Ads
        will never be placed over the room canvas, next to the editing controls, or anywhere that would
        interrupt planning a room.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
      <a href="/room-planner" class="rp-btn rp-btn-primary rp-btn-lg">
        Plan My Room
        <Icon name="arrow-right" size={18} />
      </a>
      <a href="/privacy" class="rp-btn rp-btn-secondary rp-btn-lg">Read the privacy page</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
